- **China.** Google Maps doesn''t work. Offline maps from Organic Maps or Maps.me are fine, but you''ll want Alipay or WeChat Pay set up (both now accept foreign cards since 2023) because cash is increasingly refused. A VPN installed before arrival is non-negotiable if you want Gmail.
- **India.** Offline maps handle the cities well; IRCTC train tickets need to be in the app or printed, and the app requires an Indian mobile number to register unless you book through a third party like 12Go.
- **Schengen Europe.** Pretty forgiving. Most trains (SNCF, Trenitalia, DB, Renfe) accept PDFs. The exception is Eurostar through London St Pancras, where the e-ticket in Wallet is smoother than paper at the French border checks.
- **US national parks.** Cell service is nonexistent in most of Yellowstone, Glacier, and the backcountry of Yosemite. Download the free NPS app''s offline content for the specific park before you drive in, plus AllTrails Pro ($36/year) for offline trail maps.

